##* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalm|17|1|page=654|column=1|passage=Heare the right, O {{smallcaps|Lord}}, '''attend''' vnto my crie, giue eare vnto my prayer, ''that goeth'' not out of fained lips.}}
##* {{RQ:Homer Pope Iliad|volume=I|book=I|page=4|lines=61–62|passage=Thus ''Chryſes'' pray’d: the fav’ring Povv’r '''attends''', / And from ''Olympus''’s lofty Tops deſcends.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=William Robert Wake|chapter=[[w:Psalm 31|Psalm XXXI]]|title=A Liberal Version of the {{w|Psalms}} into Modern Language, According to the Liturgy Translation;{{nb...|with Copious Notes and Illustrations, Partly Original, and Partly Selected from the Best Commentators: Calculated to Render the Book of Psalms Intelligible to Every Capacity.}}|location=Bath, Somerset|publisher={{...|Printed by}} R. Cruttwell; and sold by [[w:George Robinson (bookseller)|G[eorge] G[eorge] J[ohn] and J. Robinson]],{{nb...|Pater-noster-Row}}; and [[w:Charles Dilly|C[harles] Dilly]],{{nb...|Poultry, London.}}|year=1793|volume=I|section=verses 24–25|page=75|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Q6w7vNvZ7OIC&pg=PA75|oclc=874279270|passage=VVhilſt I vvas haſtening in my flight, I ſaid, "I am rejected from thy favour." Nevertheleſs thou '''attendedſt''' to my petition, vvhen I invoked thee.}}
