##* {{RQ:Browne Hydriotaphia|page=78|passage=Ægyptian ingenuity vvas more unſatisfied, contriving their bodies in ſvveet conſiſtences, to '''attend''' the return of their ſouls. But all vvas vanity, feeding the vvinde, and folly.}}
##* {{RQ:Dryden Indian Emperour|scene=ii|page=29|passage=Three days I promis'd to '''attend''' my Doom, / And tvvo long days and nights are yet to come: {{...}}}}
